course: dictionary
lesson: 14887
title: Words that show how a body is held
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how a person or thing is positioned. «Reclining» means leaning or lying back in a relaxed way. «Grandpa was reclining on the sofa with his eyes closed.» The clues are eyes closed and relaxed, so he is lying back, not sitting up straight.
explain: The word also describes things that tip back. «The bus seat was reclining, so I could rest my head.» A reclining seat can be moved back, so its back tips. Test your meaning in the sentence: "The bus seat was leaning back, so I could rest my head." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Reclining is part of a verb family: recline, reclines, reclined, reclining. «The cat reclines in the sun every afternoon.» Here reclines is a verb, because the cat is doing something: leaning back and relaxing.
fact: Reclining means leaning or lying back in a relaxed way.
fact: «Reclining» can describe a person, a seat or a chair that tips back.
fact: Recline is the verb: I recline, she reclines, he reclined, they are reclining.
fact: In art, «a reclining figure» is a statue or painting of a person lying back. The sculptor Henry Moore made many famous reclining figures.
fact: Planes, coaches and some sofas have reclining seats, so people can rest more comfortably.
exercise: «The reclining figure in the gallery looked calm and peaceful.» What does reclining mean here? | Hidden under a blanket | Standing up very straight | Running fast | *Lying back in a relaxed way
exercise: «Dad put the reclining seat back so he could nap.» What does the seat do? | *It tips back | It folds into a table | It spins round | It lights up
exercise: «The cat reclined on the warm rug.» Find and copy the verb. | rug | *reclined | sat | warm
test: «The sofa has a reclining back, so you can lean right back.» What does reclining describe? | A bright light | A loud bell | *A part of the sofa that tips back | A hard wooden table
test: «Grandma reclines in her garden chair with a book.» Which word is the verb? | *Reclines | Book | Chair | Garden
exam: «The statue shows a reclining figure, lying back with one arm raised.» What is a reclining figure? | A tall tower | A small bird | *A person shown lying back | A standing soldier
